    "id": "ctrl-control-effort-over-time",
    "title": "Control Effort (Actuator Command) Over Time",
    "field": "Robotics / Control Systems",
    "plotType": "Time-series actuator-command line plot",
    "description": "This plot traces the command signal the controller sends to the actuator (motor voltage, PWM, or current) versus time during a maneuver. Right after a setpoint change the effort spikes as the controller pushes hard to move the plant, then relaxes to the smaller steady value needed to hold position. The dashed line is the actuator's saturation limit, beyond which the hardware physically cannot go.",
